  "problem": "Express $\\frac{-22{x}^{2}+60x-26}{(x+1)(2x-4)^{2}}$ as a sum of partial fractions.\n\n| $\\frac{-22{x}^{2}+60x-26}{(x+1)(2x-4)^{2}}=$ | $-$ | {{field-1}} | $-$ | {{field-2}} | $+$ | {{field-3}} |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | $x+1$ |  | $2x-4$ |  | $(2x-4)^{2}$ |",
  "worked_solution": "Our task is to find $A,$ $B,$ and $C$ such that\n\n$$\n\\frac{-22{x}^{2}+60x-26}{(x+1)(2x-4)^{2}}=\\frac{A}{x+1}+\\frac{B}{2x-4}+\\frac{C}{(2x-4)^{2}}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $(x+1)(2x-4)^{2}$ gives\n\n$$\n-22{x}^{2}+60x-26=A(2x-4)^{2}+B(x+1)(2x-4)+C(x+1).\n$$\n\nLetting $x=-1$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-22(-1)^{2}+60(-1)-26 & =A(2(-1)-4)^{2}+B(-1+1)(2(-1)-4)+C(-1+1) \\\\ -108 & =A(-6)^{2} \\\\ A & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=2$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-22(2)^{2}+60(2)-26 & =A(2\\cdot 2-4)^{2}+B(2+1)(2\\cdot 2-4)+C(2+1) \\\\ 6 & =C(3) \\\\ C & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, letting $x=0$ and using our values for $A$ and $C$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-22(0)^{2}+60(0)-26 & =A(2\\cdot 0-4)^{2}+B(0+1)(2\\cdot 0-4)+2(0+1) \\\\ -26 & =(-3)(16)+B(1)(-4)+2 \\\\ -26 & =-46-4B \\\\ B & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{-22{x}^{2}+60x-26}{(x+1)(2x-4)^{2}}=-\\,\\frac{3}{x+1}-\\,\\frac{5}{2x-4}+\\frac{2}{(2x-4)^{2}}.\n$$",
